<p>NASA has completed a flight readiness review and cleared Artemis II—its first crewed flight around the Moon in more than 50 years—for an April launch attempt, as early as April 1, from Florida’s Kennedy Space Center. The Space Launch System rocket and Orion capsule are set to roll out to the launch pad next week as teams wrap up remaining closeout work. The mission will carry four astronauts: three Americans (Reid Wiseman, Victor Glover and Christina Koch) and one Canadian (Jeremy Hansen). NASA officials say they are pushing toward the April 1 target after technical issues forced the schedule to slip from an earlier plan.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/e4oh5h8vGLKHGsxGhBcKcguqMmCFTFege3NeBN6CADaj1JchQUMJlKtLQxn7eKY15NpBNNVtJKlGgWY6RuJnHXMgisGgkO5ocAsRpc0aWRWrqUykxEzPH8YGRpYbSNmsYbEsoalJXCj-HF6jo2kpQIzJZWI2sCNWG_6qPqFnJWyrkVCUsT-P' alt='NASA’s Artemis II Space Launch System rocket ahead of planned April rollout and launch preparations.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Repairs milestone: NASA cleared Artemis II after finishing its latest round of repairs ahead of an April launch attempt.</li><li>Next milestone: NASA plans to roll the rocket and spacecraft to Pad 39B on March 19, once the remaining closeout work is done.</li><li>Rocket scale: NASA’s rollout plans put the Artemis II launch vehicle at about 98 metres (322 feet) tall.</li><li>Wider timing context: SCMP noted the late-March/early-April window overlaps with a planned US President Donald Trump trip to China at the end of March.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>NASA leadership: Senior NASA officials said the agency is “on track” for an April 1 launch attempt after completing the flight readiness review, while stressing there is still work to finish before that date. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/mar/13/nasa-artemis-ii-moon-mission-launch-april'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Timing/geopolitics angle (SCMP): SCMP pointed out that the end-of-March to early-April launch period lines up with a slated visit by US President Donald Trump to China to meet President Xi. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3346456/nasa-clears-artemis-moon-rocket-april-launch-4-astronauts'>SCMP</a>)</li><li>International partner (Canada): Canadian astronaut Jeremy Hansen flying alongside three Americans underscores the mission’s multinational crew. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/sci-tech/science/nasa-clears-its-artemis-2-moon-rocket-for-april-launch-with-four-astronauts/article70737717.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3346456/nasa-clears-artemis-moon-rocket-april-launch-4-astronauts'>Nasa clears Artemis moon rocket for an April launch with 4 astronauts</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/shorts/nasa-says-its-ready-to-go-back-to-the-moon-for-the-first-time-in-50-years/article70738595.ece'>NASA says it’s ready to go back to the moon for the first time in 50 years</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/13/nasa-sets-april-1-for-artemis-ii-first-crewed-moon-mission-in-over-50-years'>NASA sets April 1 for Artemis II, first crewed Moon mission in over 50 years</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/science/2026/mar/13/nasa-artemis-ii-moon-mission-launch-april'>Nasa ‘on track’ for Artemis II moon mission launch as soon as 1 April</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/artemis-ii-launch-on-track-for-as-soon-as-april-says-nasa/a-76339333'>Artemis II launch &#x27;on track&#x27; for as soon as April, says NASA</a> - dw.com</li></ul>